      "thinking": "The design mandates the card but the real outage is third-party; still, the guidance pushes toward a fix that would've spared users pain, so I'm leaning toward degrading the account page gracefully\u2014rendering spend, statement, and basket even when the card is unavailable, rather than failing the whole page. Checkout is different since it truly needs the card, but the account page shouldn't be held hostage by that same requirement.\n\nI'm also eyeing that ~2045ms p50 latency figure, wondering if it reflects the provider's slow 503 responses and whether a timeout is even configured on the caller side\u2014worth checking how ask_the_provider is wired into the endpoints. The existing test explicitly expects the current failing behavior though, which pulls against softening it, so this is a genuine judgment call between respecting third-party outage boundaries and reducing unnecessary blast radius for users.\n\n",
